   "text": "In 1877 two dykes of auriferous diorite were discovered on the north bank of the Yarra at Warrandyte, causing a small boom with First Hill, Pig Tail, Fourth Hill, Crown and Northern companies. Pig Tail worked to 150 ft with yields up to 8 oz/ton and prospectors were said to net 6,000 pounds; the reef was cut off by a slide at about water level.",
