   "id": 278,
   "text": "The Society's page states that Louis Michel was the first person to discover gold in Australia, at Anderson Creek, Warrandyte. This is a local-heritage claim; other finds, such as Hargraves at Ophir in 1851, are usually credited as the first payable discovery.",
   "date": "1851",
   "place": "Anderson's Creek",
