   "source": "Warrandyte Historical Society (Victorian Collections)",
   "quote": "Louis Michel was the first person to discover gold in Australia. He did so in Anderson Creek, Warrandyte.",
   "corrections": [
    "Keep the claim attributed to the Society's page, not as established fact. Michel is credited with Victoria's first goldfield (1851), not the first gold in Australia.",
    "Keep it attributed to the Society: it says Michel was the first to find gold in Australia, which is a local-heritage overstatement. Michel is better described as the discoverer of Victoria's first goldfield (Anderson's Creek, 1851).",
    "Louis Michel (with partners) found gold at Anderson's Creek, Warrandyte, in mid-1851. This is commonly cited as among the first payable gold discoveries in Victoria. The Society's \"first in Australia\" wording is a local-heritage claim and is not the usual attribution."
   ],
