   "text": "Auriferous dykes are known at Diamond Creek, Warrandyte, Templestowe and Kinglake. Junner described arsenopyrite with cruciform twinning from the 'Diamond Creek Dyke', and an earlier Diamond Creek report by him appeared in Proc. Roy. Soc. Victoria in 1912.",
